const page = {
  title: "Scientific, Regulatory & Compliance Statement",
  h1: "Scientific, Regulatory & Compliance Statement",
  description: "Effective Date: May 8, 2026Last Updated: May 8, 2026",
  canonical: "/scientific-regulatory-compliance-statement/",
  author: "",
  date: "",
};
const hreflang = "<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"en-US\" href=\"https://aviantestpro.com/scientific-regulatory-compliance-statement/\" /> <link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"en\" href=\"https://aviantestpro.com/scientific-regulatory-compliance-statement/\" /> <link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ar\" href=\"https://aviantestpro.com/ar/scientific-regulatory-compliance-statement/\" /> <link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ja\" href=\"https://aviantestpro.com/ja/scientific-regulatory-compliance-statement/\" /> <link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ko-KR\" href=\"https://aviantestpro.com/ko/scientific-regulatory-compliance-statement/\" /> <link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ko\" href=\"https://aviantestpro.com/ko/scientific-regulatory-compliance-statement/\" /> <link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"es-ES\" href=\"https://aviantestpro.com/es/scientific-regulatory-compliance-statement/\" /> <link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"es\" href=\"https://aviantestpro.com/es/scientific-regulatory-compliance-statement/\" /> <link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"fr-FR\" href=\"https://aviantestpro.com/fr/scientific-regulatory-compliance-statement/\" /> <link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"fr\" href=\"https://aviantestpro.com/fr/scientific-regulatory-compliance-statement/\" /> <link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"de-DE\" href=\"https://aviantestpro.com/de/scientific-regulatory-compliance-statement/\" /> <link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"de\" href=\"https://aviantestpro.com/de/scientific-regulatory-compliance-statement/\" /> <link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"x-default\" href=\"https://aviantestpro.com/scientific-regulatory-compliance-statement/\" />";
---
<BaseLayout title={page.title} hreflang={hreflang} description={page.description} canonical={page.canonical} ogType="article">
  <article class="page-content">
    <h1 class="page-title">{page.h1}</h1>
    
    <div class="entry-content" set:html={`<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-7387b849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex"><div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> May 8, 2026<br><strong>Last Updated:</strong> May 8, 2026</p><p>Aviantestpro is committed to maintaining responsible scientific communication, lawful laboratory practices, operational transparency, and international compliance standards in connection with our website, laboratory-related services, avian DNA testing activities, and related scientific support operations.</p><p>This Scientific, Regulatory &amp; Compliance Statement explains the principles, limitations, intended use, and compliance position associated with the content and services provided through this website.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>1. Intended Scope of Services</h2><p>Aviantestpro focuses exclusively on:</p><ul><li>Avian DNA testing</li><li>Bird genetic identification</li><li>Bird sex identification testing</li><li>Avian molecular biology support</li><li>Non-human laboratory analysis</li><li>Educational and scientific laboratory services</li><li>Research-related laboratory workflows</li><li>Animal-related biological testing support</li></ul><p>Our services are intended solely for lawful non-human applications.</p><p>Aviantestpro does not provide:</p><ul><li>Human clinical testing</li><li>Human medical diagnostics</li><li>Human disease screening</li><li>Human genetic diagnosis</li><li>Human therapeutic services</li><li>Human healthcare services</li><li>Human reproductive testing</li><li>Human pharmaceutical treatment services</li></ul><p>All services described on this website are intended exclusively for non-human applications.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>2. Scientific and Laboratory Standards</h2><p>Aviantestpro aims to follow commercially reasonable laboratory practices and scientific handling procedures appropriate for avian and non-human biological analysis.</p><p>Depending on the service type, laboratory activities may involve:</p><ul><li>Molecular biology methodologies</li><li>DNA extraction procedures</li><li>PCR or qPCR workflows</li><li>Genetic marker analysis</li><li>Species-related biological identification</li><li>Sample tracking and quality-control procedures</li><li>Laboratory documentation systems</li></ul><p>Testing methodologies and workflows may evolve over time as scientific knowledge, laboratory technologies, and industry standards develop.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>3. Research Use and Non-Clinical Use</h2><p>Unless explicitly stated otherwise in writing, all services, reports, products, protocols, technical materials, and laboratory information are intended for:</p><ul><li>Research use</li><li>Educational use</li><li>Informational use</li><li>Laboratory use</li><li>Non-clinical applications</li><li>Non-human biological applications</li></ul><p>Services and materials are not intended for:</p><ul><li>Human in vivo use</li><li>Human clinical diagnosis</li><li>Human therapeutic use</li><li>Human medical decision-making</li><li>Human treatment planning</li></ul><p>No content on this website should be interpreted as medical advice, healthcare guidance, or clinical instruction.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>4. Regulatory Position</h2><p>Aviantestpro operates under the principle that avian DNA testing and related laboratory services should be conducted only for lawful purposes and in accordance with applicable regulations.</p><p>Users are responsible for ensuring compliance with all applicable:</p><ul><li>National laws</li><li>Regional laws</li><li>Import/export regulations</li><li>Wildlife regulations</li><li>Animal transport regulations</li><li>Biosecurity regulations</li><li>Laboratory handling requirements</li><li>Sample submission requirements</li></ul><p>Regulatory requirements may differ between jurisdictions.</p><p>Aviantestpro does not represent or guarantee that every product or service described on this website is available, permitted, or regulated identically in all countries or regions.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>5. Non-Human Testing Statement</h2><p>Aviantestpro strictly limits its laboratory-related services and scientific activities to non-human applications.</p><p>The website, reports, laboratory procedures, and technical information are intended exclusively for:</p><ul><li>Birds</li><li>Avian species</li><li>Animal-related laboratory support</li><li>Non-human biological analysis</li><li>Educational and scientific applications</li></ul><p>No services are intended for human clinical or medical use.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>6. No Diagnostic or Treatment Claims</h2><p>Information presented on this website is not intended to:</p><ul><li>Diagnose disease</li><li>Prevent disease</li><li>Cure disease</li><li>Treat disease</li><li>Replace professional medical advice</li><li>Replace veterinary judgment</li><li>Establish healthcare decisions</li></ul><p>Laboratory reports and technical data should be interpreted only within the context of their intended scientific or informational use.</p><p>Aviantestpro does not guarantee that laboratory findings alone are sufficient for breeding, commercial, veterinary, regulatory, or legal decision-making.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>7. Data Integrity and Sample Quality</h2><p>Laboratory outcomes may be affected by:</p><ul><li>Sample quality</li><li>Transportation conditions</li><li>Environmental exposure</li><li>Biological variability</li><li>Sample contamination</li><li>Incomplete submissions</li><li>Technical limitations</li></ul><p>While commercially reasonable quality-control procedures may be used, no laboratory process can eliminate all sources of uncertainty.</p><p>Users are responsible for ensuring proper sample collection, handling, labeling, packaging, and shipment.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>8. Compliance with Search Engine and Platform Policies</h2><p>Aviantestpro aims to maintain website content and operational transparency consistent with:</p><ul><li>Search engine quality guidelines</li><li>Platform transparency standards</li><li>International privacy principles</li><li>Consumer protection expectations</li><li>Responsible scientific communication standards</li></ul><p>Website content is designed to clearly communicate:</p><ul><li>Non-human intended use</li><li>Scientific and educational purpose</li><li>Laboratory service limitations</li><li>Regulatory boundaries</li><li>Compliance-focused operational practices</li></ul><p>No content on this website should be interpreted as promoting unauthorized healthcare services, illegal biological testing, or prohibited medical activity.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>9. AI, Search, and Public Indexing</h2><p>Public content on this website may be indexed or analyzed by:</p><ul><li>Search engines</li><li>AI search systems</li><li>Automated crawlers</li><li>Language models</li><li>Web indexing technologies</li></ul><p>Publicly accessible website information is intended for educational visibility and informational communication.</p><p>Private customer submissions, confidential laboratory information, and customer-specific reports are not intentionally made publicly accessible.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>10. International Customers and Jurisdiction</h2><p>Aviantestpro may provide information and laboratory-related services to international users where legally permitted.</p><p>Users accessing this website from outside the operating jurisdiction of Aviantestpro do so at their own initiative and are responsible for compliance with local laws and regulations.</p><p>International shipment, customs, wildlife, and biosecurity restrictions may apply to biological samples and laboratory materials.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>11. Limitation of Scientific Interpretation</h2><p>Scientific interpretation may evolve over time as:</p><ul><li>Research advances</li><li>Technologies improve</li><li>Reference databases change</li><li>Industry standards develop</li><li>Regulatory expectations evolve</li></ul><p>Aviantestpro does not guarantee that all scientific information published on the website will remain permanently complete, current, or universally applicable.</p><p>Users should independently evaluate scientific and regulatory suitability for their intended use.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>12. Intellectual Property and Technical Content</h2><p>All technical descriptions, laboratory-related content, workflows, graphics, reports, documentation, and scientific materials published on this website remain protected under applicable intellectual property laws unless otherwise stated.</p><p>Unauthorized reproduction, redistribution, or commercial misuse may violate applicable laws.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>13. Updates to This Statement</h2><p>Aviantestpro reserves the right to update, modify, or revise this Scientific, Regulatory &amp; Compliance Statement at any time without prior notice.</p><p>Changes become effective immediately upon publication on this page.</p><p>Continued use of the website constitutes acceptance of any updated version.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>14. Contact Information</h2><p>For compliance, scientific communication, or regulatory-related inquiries, please contact:</p><p><strong>Aviantestpro Compliance Team</strong><br>Email: <a><span class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="b9d8ddd4d0d7f9d8cfd0d8d7cddccacdc9cbd697dad6d4">[email&#160;protected]</span></a><br>Website: <a>https://aviantestpro.com</a></p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>Recommended Related Compliance Pages</h2><p>For stronger transparency and international compliance practices, the website should also include:</p><ul><li>Privacy Policy</li><li>Disclaimer</li><li>Terms &amp; Conditions</li><li>Cookie Policy</li><li>Shipping Policy</li><li>Refund Policy</li><li>Sample Submission Policy</li><li>Research Use Only (RUO) Statement</li><li>Contact Page</li></ul><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>Recommended Transparency &amp; Compliance Features</h2><p>To strengthen international trust signals and search compliance, the following are recommended:</p><ul><li>HTTPS/SSL on all pages</li><li>Visible contact information</li><li>Clear non-human testing statements</li><li>Transparent sample handling procedures</li><li>Cookie consent management</li><li>Laboratory limitation disclosures</li><li>Structured data implementation</li><li>Accessible legal/compliance pages from every page footer</li><li>Consistent domain-matching business email addresses</li><li>Public explanation of intended service scope</li></ul></div></div></div>`} />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
